    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0022-l0000",
      "p0001-n0022-l0001",
      "p0001-n0022-l0002",
      "p0001-n0022-l0003",
      "p0001-n0022-l0004",
      "p0001-n0022-l0005",
      "p0001-n0022-l0006",
      "p0001-n0022-l0007"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Firstly, a universal thermodynamic model(UTM) of bath water is established by constructing two initial sub-equations named the Heat Differential Equation(HDE) and the Temperature Distribution(TD) respectively. Based on Fourier's law, the Stefan-Boltzmann law and the first law of thermodynamics, HDE is established, which also takes heat conduction, heat radiation and evaporation of water into account. Moreover, we get the numerical solution of TD by using the PDE tool of MATLAB, and fit its temperature distribution surface by the plane equation, whose goodness of fit is 0.931. The fitting equation is regarded as the approximate analytical solution."
  },
